%% Four systems, as the page prints them: m1-4, m5-8, m9-12, m13-16.
%%
%% \bar "||" after m8 closes the verse before the refrain (source m8
%% BarLine subtype=double). The page also prints "Refrain" over m9, but
%% no song in this repo marks one on the staff - the convention here is
%% to say "with refrain" in the meter string, as blessed-assurance does,
%% and let the lyrics carry it. The tune line on the page says the same.
%%
%% The fermata in m14 is on "me;" - a hold before the closing phrase,
%% NOT an ending fermata. The source puts one above the treble staff and
%% one below the bass (m14 fermataAbove / fermataBelow); both were
%% dropped by the converter. It goes on soprano and bass alone, since
%% one mark per staff is what the page shows and what blessed-assurance
%% does with its marks.
